      "content": "fair enough. but when you talk about \"unfounded claims\" or \"misinformation,\" does that mean there was actually no valid argument for why people should have the right to refuse medical procedures, even during a crisis? or is it more like the public health argument just naturally outweighs personal choice in these situations?",
